Answer: For a positive n, fun2(n) prints the values of n, 2n, 4n, 8n ... while the value is smaller than LIMIT. After printing values in increasing order, it prints same numbers again in reverse order. For example fun2(100) prints 100, 200, 400, 800, 800, 400, 200, 100. If n is negative, the function is returned immediately. Question 2 : Predict the output of the following program. What does the following fun() do in general?
